kosha amine

  -- amino group -NH2 attached to carbon. nitrogen with lone pair.
  -- the lone pair makes amines basic — accepts H⁺ from water.
  -- R-NH2 + H2O ⇌ R-NH3⁺ + OH⁻ (weak base)
  --
  -- primary: R-NH2. secondary: R2-NH. tertiary: R3-N. quaternary: R4-N⁺.
  -- amines have distinctive smell: fish (trimethylamine), putrefaction (cadaverine).
  --
  -- reactions:
  --   amide formation: -NH2 + -COOH → -CONH- + H2O (the peptide bond)
  --   alkylation: -NH2 + R-X → -NHR + HX
  --   acylation: -NH2 + acyl → amide
  --
  -- amino acids: contain both -NH2 and -COOH. the building blocks of proteins.
  --   at physiological pH: -NH3⁺ (protonated) and -COO⁻ (deprotonated) → zwitterion
  -- neurotransmitters: dopamine, serotonin, adrenaline — all amines.
  -- DNA bases: adenine, guanine, cytosine — all contain amino groups.
  -- aniline: C6H5-NH2. aromatic amine. dye industry.

